    <p class="text-body section-body-prose">
      Upgrading your home heating system or adding weatherization insulation is one of the highest return-on-investment improvements a Pacific Northwest homeowner can undertake. Beyond increasing year-round comfort, modern high-efficiency heat pumps provide built-in air conditioning during hot summer months and significantly reduce monthly winter utility expenses.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body section-body-prose">
      In Washington State, local electric and natural gas utilities work alongside state clean energy programs to lower upfront installation expenses. Understanding which utility serves your property is the first step toward stacking available incentives and maximizing net project savings.
    </p>
  </section>

